    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_3",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Jane M. Fearnley-Whittingstall (\"née\" Lascelles) (born 1939 in Kensington, London) is a writer and garden designer with a diploma in landscape architecture. She has won two gold medals at Chelsea Flower Show. She has two children: Sophy and Hugh, the celebrity chef, and six grandchildren. From 2005 to 2007 she wrote a weekly column about family life, in \"The Times\". She has also written for \"The Daily Telegraph\", \"Daily Mail\", \"The Oldie\", \"Woman's Weekly\", \"The Garden\", \"The English Garden\" and \"Gardens Illustrated\".",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999945336314,
